    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The full test suite consists of the two acceptance tests, both green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `registrationDate` field for owners so that it defaults to the server's current date when omitted and is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\n**Changes, each in its natural home:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, this makes the field both settable on `POST` and returned on `GET`, and the code generator produces a `LocalDate` on the DTOs (serialized by Jackson as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the mapped `registration_date` column with a `LocalDate registrationDate` property plus its accessors. MapStruct maps it automatically by name in both directions, so `OwnerMapper` needed no changes.\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 Added the default-to-today rule alongside the existing create-time logic, guarded by `owner.isNew()` so it only applies at creation and never overwrites a supplied date or disturbs updates.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column so persistence works across all supported databases (tests run on hsqldb).\n\nThe default lives at the service layer (the existing home for owner create-time business rules), the DTO/entity mapping stays in the mapper, and the shape lives in the OpenAPI contract \u2014 no class became a catch-all.",
